/* ============================================================
   GOLD CHAIN CATALOG DATA
   Real product data from the client sheet (330 SKUs). Each item
   carries its own name, product code, chain type/category,
   workmanship difficulty, image reference code, thickness, weight,
   and a REAL wholesale price for every karat (8K-24K) - already
   computed by the client from their own gold-rate + workmanship
   model, not derived by us.

   Two DIFFERENT codes exist per item - do not mix them up:
   - productCode (e.g. "AFC1"): the real catalog code, shown to
     buyers as the product code.
   - imageCode (e.g. "0001-FOR-20"): used ONLY to name photo files,
     see /public/images/README.txt.

   21 additional rows in the source sheet ("eklenen"/short-form
   difficulty labels) were left out - they have no thickness,
   weight, or image code yet, so there is nothing real to price or
   photograph for them. Add them once that data exists.

   One known data issue carried over as-is (not introduced by us):
   imageCode "0208-OUZ-60" is used by two different products in the
   client sheet (Oval Link Chain and Hallow Palm Chain), so they
   will show the same photo until the client corrects the source.
   ============================================================ */

